    <innerclass refid="classthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_sitemap_crawler" prot="public">themis::scraper::SitemapCrawler</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespacethemis">themis</innernamespace>
    <innernamespace refid="namespacethemis_1_1scraper">themis::scraper</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>XML sitemap fetching and URL extraction for sitemap-driven crawl mode. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="version"><para>1.0.0</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
<sect1 id="scraper__sitemap_8h_1autotoc_md16_1s1"><sect2 id="scraper__sitemap_8h_1autotoc_md16">
<title>Purpose</title><para>Provides <computeroutput>SitemapCrawler</computeroutput> — a lightweight XML sitemap parser that extracts <computeroutput>&lt;loc&gt;</computeroutput> URLs from standard sitemaps and sitemap index files. Supports both single-level sitemaps and two-level sitemap index files (per the sitemaps.org protocol, <ulink url="https://www.sitemaps.org/protocol.html">https://www.sitemaps.org/protocol.html</ulink>).</para>
</sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="scraper__sitemap_8h_1autotoc_md17_1s1"><sect2 id="scraper__sitemap_8h_1autotoc_md17">
<title>Supported sitemap formats</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Standard sitemap: <computeroutput>&lt;urlset&gt;&lt;url&gt;&lt;loc&gt;…&lt;/loc&gt;&lt;/url&gt;&lt;/urlset&gt;</computeroutput></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Sitemap index: <computeroutput>&lt;sitemapindex&gt;&lt;sitemap&gt;&lt;loc&gt;…&lt;/loc&gt;&lt;/sitemap&gt;&lt;/sitemapindex&gt;</computeroutput> For index files, the crawler fetches each child sitemap and merges its URLs.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The parser uses string-based <computeroutput>&lt;loc&gt;</computeroutput> extraction and does not depend on pugixml, so it functions in all build configurations.</para>
</sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="scraper__sitemap_8h_1autotoc_md18_1s1"><sect2 id="scraper__sitemap_8h_1autotoc_md18">
<title>Limits</title><para><computeroutput>max_urls_per_sitemap</computeroutput> (default: 5 000) caps how many URLs are returned to protect against memory exhaustion from very large sitemaps.</para>
</sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="scraper__sitemap_8h_1autotoc_md19_1s1"><sect2 id="scraper__sitemap_8h_1autotoc_md19">
<title>Thread safety</title><para><computeroutput>SitemapCrawler</computeroutput> is stateless between calls; each <computeroutput>fetchUrls()</computeroutput> call is independent and safe to call from a single thread.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para>src/scraper/ROADMAP.md — v1.2 feature: sitemap-driven crawl mode </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
</sect2></sect1>
